\subsection*{D.3 Topology via $C^k$ convergence}

Let $\mathrm{Emb}^k(\mathcal{S},\mathbb{R}^3)$ denote the space of
$C^k$ embeddings with the $C^k$ topology. Let $H^k(\mathcal{S})$ denote
the Sobolev space of curvature fields.

Define a topology on $\mathcal{M}$ by declaring that a sequence


\[
(\Phi_n, H_n) \to (\Phi, H)
\]


if and only if:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item $\Phi_n \to \Phi$ in the $C^k$ topology,
  \item $H_n \to H$ in the weak $H^k$ topology,
  \item the PDE residuals converge:
  

\[
  \kappa \Delta H_n + \mu H_n - \lambda H_n^3 \to 0
  \quad \text{in } H^{k-2}.
  \]


\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{D.4 Quotient topology}

The moduli space inherits the quotient topology:


\[
\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{top}}
=
\left( \mathrm{Emb}^k(\mathcal{S},\mathbb{R}^3)
       \times H^k(\mathcal{S}) \right) / \!\sim.
\]



\subsection*{D.5 Connected components}

Under this topology, the moduli space decomposes into seven connected
components:


\[
\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{top}}
=
\bigsqcup_{i=1}^{7} \mathcal{M}_i,
\]


each corresponding to one canonical curvature object $\mathcal{V}_i$.

