\mathcal{T}_1 \cup_{\sim} \mathcal{T}_2 \cup_{\sim} \mathcal{T}_3.
\]



\subsection*{E.2 PDE solution on each cell}

We seek a steady-state solution of


\[
\kappa \Delta H + \mu H - \lambda H^3 = 0.
\]



Because the gluing pattern is symmetric under a 3-cycle, we assume


\[
H|_{\mathcal{T}_i} = H_0 \quad \text{constant}.
\]



Substituting into the PDE gives the algebraic equation:


\[
\mu H_0 - \lambda H_0^3 = 0.
\]



Thus the nontrivial solutions are:


\[
H_0 = \pm \sqrt{\frac{\mu}{\lambda}}.
\]



We choose the positive branch for definiteness:


\[
H_0 = \sqrt{\frac{\mu}{\lambda}}.
\]



\subsection*{E.3 Boundary compatibility}

Because $H$ is constant on each cell:


\[
H|_{\gamma_{i,j}} = H_0,
\qquad
\partial_\nu H|_{\gamma_{i,j}} = 0.
\]



Thus the gluing conditions


\[
H_i = H_j \circ \psi,
\qquad
\partial_\nu H_i = (\partial_\nu H_j) \circ \psi
\]


are automatically satisfied.

\subsection*{E.4 Embedding into $\mathbb{R}^3$}

Define the embedding:


\[
\Phi(x,y) = (X(x,y), Y(x,y), Z(x,y)),
\qquad
Z(x,y) = H_0.
\]



Thus the entire object lies on the horizontal plane $Z = H_0$.

The in-plane coordinates $(X,Y)$ are obtained by gluing the three
hooked triangles along their boundary arcs. Because the gluing pattern
