  \item satisfies the PDE,
  \item satisfies boundary compatibility,
  \item embeds smoothly into $\mathbb{R}^3$,
  \item has computable curvature invariants,
  \item and is minimal.
\end{itemize}

Therefore $\mathcal{V}_1$ is a valid canonical curvature object.
